Combining Excalibur with either katana or silver saber is an
ascendable combination.  Either is better than the twohanded
curse trap that comes with the bell.

Long sword skill class to skilled, two handed to skilled, both
are enhancements to be considered early on by a Samurai.

> What are your experiences/preferences as weapons for Samurai?

Missiles *matter*.  Once you can bless your stack of ya and max
out your luck it becomes time to enhance bow all the way up to
expert as soon as you can.  For that matter I like to spend a skill
slot on dagger first thing to have a good missile choice that does
not disappear when thrown.  Then alternating among long sword,
my secondary melee wield (silver saber as soon as one comes
available or katana in the long sword skill class before that).

My skill slot order goes something like dagger to basic by the
first couple of levels of the mines, mixing long sword and two
weapon to skilled by the end of the mines, bow to expert as
soon as my luck is maxed out from an altar, then whatever else
comes to mind later.  An XP=30 Samurai I am running in vanilla
is expert at bow, long sword, two weapon, martial arts, skilled
at broadsword and polearm, basic at dagger, saber, pickaxe
and shuriken.  Foocubi dancing rules.

> I'd also
> like to hear what you usually use as weapon in the Endgame, I was
> thinking about twoweapon Grayswandir/Frostbrand or the like with
> katana/silver saber--any other recommendations or suggestions?

Grayswandir is the best general purpose melee weapon in the game.
If you have it, it justifies switching to it almost independent of
what
other main melee weapon you were using before.

Frost Brand gives good damage but explodes potions.  I will use it
if I don't have Excalibur but I won't switch from Excalibur to it.


